<title>USA: Provident files for 5.9mln shares.</title>
<headline>Provident files for 5.9mln shares.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Provident Cos Inc filed Thursday with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission a registration statement for up to 5,917,500 of its shares which will be offered by Textron Inc.</p>
<p>The insurance company said underwriters for the secondary offering are Morgan Stanley &amp; Co and Salomon Brothers Inc.</p>
<p>Textron acquired the shares as part of Provident's acquisition of Paul Revere Corp, according to the SEC filing.</p>
<p>Under the terms of the Paul Revere acquisition, Textron received $20 per share in cash and $6 per share in Provident common stock.</p>
</text>
